A||N||38||Fiero5||50 Fun Things To Do To Telemarketers||||12||
Z||000000||Fiero5||05-23-2001||12:09 PM||||50 Fun Things To Do To Telemarketers<P>1. Talk really fast.<BR>2. Turn on the TV.   Change the channel to one that only gets<BR>static.  Turn the volume up really loud.  Say that you can't hear<BR>them over the static.<BR>3. Make up your own language.  Speak it.<BR>4. Hang up.<BR>5. Make up a one word language.  Speak it.<BR>6. Say, "This phone line is for emergency use only.  Do you have<BR>an emergency?"<BR>7. If they say "Yes" to number 6 say, "Please state the nature of<BR>the emergency."  Then insist that their emergency isn't an<BR>emergency.  Hang up.<BR>8. If they say "No" to number 6 say, "I'm sorry but this line is<BR>for emergencies only."  Hang up.<BR>9. Pretend you just took hostages, and make demands.<BR>10. Pretend that you are a hostage negotiator, and try to get the<BR>telemarketer to release the hostages.<BR>11. Order a large pepperoni pizza, some garlic bread, and a<BR>meatball sub.<BR>12. Pretend that your phone line is an automatic phone sex line.<BR>13. Dial the phone and say, "Hey!  I lent you 50 bucks.  You<BR>better pay up or else I'm gonna come over there and hurt you! "<BR>14. Repeatedly dial the phone.  Mutter that it isn't ringing.<BR>15. Claim to be the mafia.<BR>16. Say, "Moe's tavern Moe speaking."<BR>17. Say something that Moe would say to Bart after Bart makes a<BR>prank call.<BR>18. Ask him/her if he/she would like a magazine or newspaper<BR>subscription.<BR>19. Ask the telemarketer to find your friend Mike last name<BR>Rotch.  Claim you will only buy a subscription from them.<BR>20. Say, "Oh no! It's the Feds!  They're on to us!"<BR>21. Claim to be the FBI.  Say, "This is the Federal Bureau of<BR>Investigation. How may I help you?"<BR>22. Dial *69.  Wait about a minute and say, "Damn unreliable<BR>*69."<BR>23. Speak a foreign language.<BR>24. If you do # 24 and the telemarketer gets a person who speaks<BR>the language you used, speak another language, use a made up<BR>language, or say that you were speaking English the whole time.<BR>25. Pretend that the telemarketer is your husband/wife or<BR>boyfriend/girlfriend.  Talk sexually, making references to what<BR>you are going to do to him/her later tonight.  When you "realize"<BR>that you are not speaking to your<BR>husband/wife/boyfriend/girlfriend yell, "Pervert!" Slam the phone<BR>down to hang up.<BR>26. Say, "Help! I'm being robbed! He's got a gun!"<BR>27. Communicate only through Morse code.<BR>28. Talk to the telemarketer.  During the conversation dial the<BR>phone, and ask for Bill.  Do this repeatedly.<BR>29. Try to sell the telemarketer something.<BR>30. Act drunk.<BR>31. Turn on your shower.  Say that you are on a portable phone<BR>and are really late for an important meeting.  Scream as though<BR>you were electrocuted.<BR>32. Ask him/her if he/she can smell bacon.  Insist that there is<BR>a strong scent of bacon over the phone.<BR>33. Ask if he/she has been to Australia.  Regardless of his/her<BR>answer ask if you can buy a boomerang and didgeridoo.<BR>34. If he/she says "No" to #36 insist that he/she buy yours.<BR>35. If he/she says "Yes" to #36 ask if he/she will take a strange<BR>currency.<BR>36. Pretend to be an escaped mental patient.  Mutter things like,<BR>"They'll never catch me again," "No! Not the jacket! No, no, no!"<BR>After saying one of these mutter incoherently.<BR>37. Make him/her dance for a sale.  Claim that you won't buy<BR>because you couldn't see him/her dance.<BR>38. Make him/her sing to get a sale.<BR>39. If a male sings for #38, claim that he sounds like Brittany<BR>Spears.<BR>40. If a female sings for #38, claim that she sounds like Barry<BR>White.<BR>41. Pretend to be really interested.  Then say, "No."<BR>42. Engage him/her in an "intellectual" conversation on an<BR>extremely boring subject.<BR>43. Say nothing until he/she hangs up.<BR>44. Say, "I told you.  I don't know where your dog is!"  Then<BR>hang up.<BR>45. Keep crackers near the phone.  When a telemarketer calls eat<BR>the crackers.  Chew loudly, make slurping noises, and talk with<BR>your mouth full. If you want pretend that you are choking.<BR>46. After he/she hangs up, use *69 or Caller ID to get the phone<BR>number. Call the telemarketer.<BR>47. Ask the telemarketer for his/her home phone number.  Claim<BR>that you need some time to think, and that you'll get back to<BR>them.<BR>48. If he/she is selling a newspaper or magazine, go on and on<BR>about how great another newspaper/magazine is.<BR>49. Pretend you are a telemarketer from a rival company.  Get<BR>him/her to buy your product.<BR>50. Say, "Yes" immediately to whatever they are selling and hang<BR>up immediately afterwards.<BR><P>------------------<BR>                     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero1sig.JPG">                   <BR>http://www.kelleyfamilyfieros.homestead.com/index.html||||reg||12
Z||000001||JSocha||05-23-2001||12:25 PM||||I just simply tell the tellemarketer, <B>"I'm getting bored right now.  I will, however, like to hand you over so you can talk to one of my dogs who might be less interested then I am."</B><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||7
Z||000002||KnightRyder31||05-23-2001||12:32 PM||||HAHAHAHA!<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fiero5||05-23-2001||12:34 PM||||Another thing that is fun is to say, "Hey, have you heard this one yet?" and tell them a stupid joke. Then say, gotta go-see ya.<P>Here is a good one that is pretty short:<BR> <P>70-year old George went for his annual physical. <BR>All of his tests came back with normal results. <P>Dr. Smith said, "George, everything looks great physically. How are you <BR>doing mentally and emotionally? Are you at peace with yourself, and do you <BR>have a good relationship with God? <P>George replied, "God and me are tight. He knows I have poor eyesight, so <BR>he's fixed it so that when I get up in the middle of the night to go to the <BR>bathroom (poof) the light goes on, when I'm done (poof) the light goes off. <P>"Wow!" commented Dr. Smith, "That's incredible!" <P>A little later in the day Dr. Smith called George's wife. <P>"Ethel," he said, "I just wanted to let you know that George is doing fine. Physically he's great. I also wanted to ask, as I am in awe of his relationship with God. Is it true that he gets up during the night and (poof) the light goes on in the bathroom, and <BR>then when he is through (poof) the light goes off?" <P>Ethel exclaimed, "Oh, my God! He's peeing in the refrigerator again!"<P>------------------<BR>                     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero1sig.JPG">                   <BR>http://www.kelleyfamilyfieros.homestead.com/index.html||||reg||10
Z||000004||Raydar||05-23-2001||01:13 PM||||Caller ID is a wonderful thing.<P>If I get a call from a telemarketer, I call back. <BR>It's usually into the <I>outgoing</I> line of a PBX. <BR>It doesn't ring. It just connects. This ties up their system because they can't get a dialtone. I can actually hear the moron going off hook repeatedly. They never figure out what's going on. I've even yelled at a few of them. They get <I>soooo</I> confused.<BR>Geek stuff, but fun, nevertheless.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 black Formula<BR>88 Duke coupe <BR>88 "wadded up" Formula (parts car)<p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 05-23-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000005||Oreif||05-23-2001||01:46 PM||||Just get "Pivacy Manager". Never even rings the phone. When they call they have to state their name and business. Some try to call thru but you just hit the #3 and they get told to remove me from the call list.<P>Before we had PM I use to look at the caller I D and answer the phone:<BR>"Yes, I'd like to order a large pepperoni pizza"<BR>They usually say "This isn't a pizza place"<BR>Then I'd say" Oops, sorry I must have mis-dialed" then hang up.<P>It takes them a few momments to realize they were the ones that called you!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>||||reg||14
Z||000006||rogergarrison||05-23-2001||01:56 PM||||play a porno video really loud, leave phone off the hook and go away.||||reg||1
Z||000007||FieroLisa||05-23-2001||01:56 PM||||Then theres always when they ask for someone else, or even you, say "Hold on a sec let me get him/her" Then you just walk away, put them on hold and wait till they hang up.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Ken Wittlief||05-23-2001||01:58 PM||||My favorite gag to screw with someones head on the phone. When it rings pick it up but dont say anything.<P>  after a few seconds the person that is calling you will say, "Hello?!"<P>  now turn the call around and pretend you are calling them, and say, Hi, is Ken there? (use your own name).<P>  the fact that they called you but somehow now you are calling them, and you are asking for the person they called to ask for, totally blows them out of the water. they will be wondering for the next three days how they received a phone call made to your number from someone else calling for you.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Ken Wittlief||05-23-2001||02:01 PM||||if they start asking questions or if you get the chance, say "is this 555-1234 (use your number - the number they dialed).<P>  insist that you just picked up the phone and dialed that number trying to reach 'yourself' and they answered the phone.<P>  if they call back - do it again, and say "what the hell is going on? who is this? what have you done with Ken? Im calling 911!"||||reg||1
Z||000010||Wade87GT||05-23-2001||02:08 PM||||In Florida, you can pay the state 7 dollars a year and they'll pull your number from all of the telemarketeers phone lists. It takes about 6 to 8 months to go into effect. In over 8 years, I've received maybe 4 TM calls. Those times I just read from the letter (kept in the drawer nest to the phone) which informs them of their illegal call and to please remove me from their list. Before that I used a little electronic device called "The Last Word". You hold it in the background a bit, push the button and it plays either, "Eat shxt!, F%#k You!, F%#*ing Jerk!, You're an As#$%le! If you hold the button down, it keeps repeating the last played comment. Had fun with that one.||||reg||3
Z||000011||JSocha||05-23-2001||02:46 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><B>"what the hell is going on? who is this? what have you done with Ken? Im calling 911!"</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>"Hey!  They got Kenny!" Those b@st@rds!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000012||JSocha||05-23-2001||02:51 PM||||Or you all can go to:  <A HREF="http://www.essential.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.esentials.com</A><P><B>EDITED 5/23/01 @ 2:20PM CDT:</B>  Just went to the site and then called them.  They no longer offer this service but support exsisting customers who subscribed when it was available.  Yet you can't change the information...go figure!<P>They "did" send you a package (for FREE) that you filled out and sent back to them.  They then (again for FREE) would submit the information to a "REMOVAL" database of hundreds of companies to make sure your name does not appear on their listings.<P>Takes about 3 to 6 months before you see the results.  <P>We Did this before we moved and by the time we moved, we had no more annoying late evening calls from telemarketers.  Now with a new phone number, its starting all over again and I just requested Essentials packet again.  Also, junk mail in our mail box (you know, credit card solicitations, etc. went from 20 a week to nill).<P>It was a good service while it lasted...<P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> <p>[This message has been edited by JSocha (edited 05-23-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000013||Fiero5||05-23-2001||03:28 PM||||I just found this on the web. It's pretty funny!<BR>_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-<BR>Getting back at Telemarketers<BR>Our biggest disappointment with Caller ID was that many phone calls were tagged "OUT OF AREA" rather than giving a phone number. In particular, banks of phones behind switchboards or in a Centrex are marked that way, which covers most of those pesky telemarketers that make our lives so miserable.<P>We've found a way to work around that which others with Caller ID may also wish to use.<P>When we get calls marked OUT OF AREA, especially at the prime telemarketer time (6-8 pm), we now answer the phone "KDNA, you're on the air!" Usually the telemarketer will be a bit befuddled, and ask for one of us by name. We will repeat that we are a radio station, that the caller is on the air, and is, in fact, the twenty-fifth caller.<P>Here's a dialog with one telemarketer who bit real hard:<P>Me: (seeing OUT OF AREA on Caller ID, using bouncy DJ voice) KDNA, you're<BR>   on the air!<BR>Telemarketer: May I speak to Mad-uh-LEEN So...So...So-johr-NOHR?<BR>M:  This is KDNA, and you are ON THE AIR!  You've just won your choice of<BR>   a new Ford Explorer or $25,000 in cash!!!<BR>T: I have?<BR>M: You certainly have.<BR>T: Oh my god!<BR>M: Happy?  Which will it be, the Explorer or the money?<BR>T: I don't know!  Let me get my supervisor!<BR>M: You don't need your supervisor, it's your prize.  Are you calling us from<BR>   work?<BR>T: Yes I am.  (background voices)  My boss says to take the money.<BR>M: The money!  So you listen to KDNA while you're working?<BR>T: I didn't even know we were calling you!<BR>M: Well, where are you calling us from?<BR>T: (some place thousands of miles from us)<BR>M: My, my!  I guess you can't pick us up all the way out there!  So what's<BR>   your name?<BR>T: Sherry.<BR>M: Sherry, tell us here on KDNA what kind of music you like.<BR>T: I'm so nervous I can't even think!  Nothing like this has ever happened<BR>   to me!<BR>M: Sherry, if you like the kind of music that we play here on KDNA, we'll<BR>   play one just for you!<BR>T: But I wouldn't be able to hear it.  Where's your radio station, anyway?<BR>M: We're broadcasting out of Silicon Valley, California, at 106.6 FM.<BR>   [obviously telemarketer isn't smart enough to know FM stations don't end<BR>   in even decimals.]<BR>T: This is just so great!<BR>M: Sherry, how old are you?<BR>T: I'm 20.<BR>M: And what do you do?<BR>T: I'm a business student at (some college).<BR>M: What will you do with the money, Sherry?  Start a business?<BR>T: Oh, I just don't know!<BR>M: I thought you said you were at work, Sherry.<BR>T: I am.  This is to help pay for college.<BR>M: What's your job?<BR>T: I'm a telemarketer.<BR>M: You're a WHAT?<BR>T: I'm a telemarketer...  I call people up and ask them if they want to buy<BR>   (product/service/etc)<BR>M: Oh, that's too bad.<BR>T: Why?<BR>M: Because we here at KDNA think telemarketers are the lowest scum on earth,<BR>   and I don't think we can give this prize to a telemarketer.  You folks<BR>   are always interrupting people during dinner and I think that's rotten.<BR>   So I don't think you should win.<BR>T: But that's not fair!<BR>M: Of course not!  But hey, it's my radio show, I get to make the rules.<BR>T: But you can't do that!<BR>M: I sure can, I'm giving this prize to the next caller.  Meanwhile, I<BR>   suggest you quit your job.  Today.<BR>&lt;byline.gif&gt;<BR>Written by: Unknown<BR><P>------------------<BR>                     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero1sig.JPG">                   <BR>http://www.kelleyfamilyfieros.homestead.com/index.html||||reg||10
Z||000014||Cooter||05-23-2001||03:33 PM||||I have a program on my computer that you track the TM calls with. It has a list of questions and with each question it has the FTC law regarding telemarketing. You just type in the info when they give tell it. They are required to give you their full name, tell if the call is a solicitation, the complete name of their company, a "real" contact phone number, the name of the on-duty supervisor, whether or not they have an established "do not call policy" (and a reminder that there is a fine to pay if they do not have a policy), you can then request to be added to their do not call list and request a copy of the company's no call policy- it takes about 3 minutes to do and if they ever call back, you have a documented time, date and contact person that should have added you to the no call list. I like it when they try to not answer the questions, I just say "according to Federal Law #########, you are required to provide this information." Then the supervisors get on the line and the real fun starts  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000015||fropuff||05-23-2001||03:38 PM||||If you listen to Bob and Tom, this was on:<P>&gt;One time, a telemarketer called to sell cemetary plots.  The guy pretended he was depressed and suicidal.  He was saying how he was divorced, he was fired from his job, etc.  He told the telemarketer he had a gun and was going to kill himself.  The telemarketer didn't know what to do, but still tried to sell his plot.  The guy made a noise that sounded like he shot himself, then didn't say anything.  I don't know what the telemarketer did...||||reg||1
Z||000016||JSocha||05-23-2001||04:07 PM||||Cooter, what's the name of the program and where did (or can) you get it from?<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000017||Cooter||05-23-2001||05:20 PM||||The program is called Enigma and I found it on cNet's download pages. ||||reg||1
Z||000018||DaRkLoRD||05-23-2001||05:28 PM||||One of my friends brothers has a job as a telemarketer, and on his first day of the job, he called each person using a different fake accent.. sounded pretty funny!<P>once I got called by a telemarketing survey about various kinds of soft drinks.. eventually I just started saying "pepsi" to every question, no matter what it was.. finally the guy asked me why I liked pepsi so much, and I just said "cuz they got the spice girls!". (this was pre-britney) at that point I hung up...<P>------------------<BR>   <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>   <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||12
Z||000019||beer_stud_21||05-23-2001||06:35 PM||||The last telemarketer I talked to was trying to sell me "Hawaii Tribune Hearald" newspapers from somewhere in alabama or gerogia or some place like that.  When I finally figured out she wasn't even on the island I just told her "I'll be glad to talk to you for as long as you want but im not going to buy anything."  then she said  "Well, I have a million other calls to make. "-click   Not quite as clever as some of the ones above, but worked great.<P>-Marlin||||reg||1
Z||000020||DJRice||05-23-2001||10:21 PM||||I listened to an entire pitch on vynil siding and then told the telemarketer that It sounded very good and my apartment could use some work outside, but that I would have to check it out with my landlord....He then asked "You live in an apartment?"  I replied "Yes."<BR>He then said "If you live in an apartment, then you are not eligible for this offer."<BR>I then asked "So why are you wasting my time with this then?"<P>And he hung up.<P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/djr_signature.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000021||Robert||05-23-2001||11:37 PM||||On the up side of calls during dinner, over 3 years ago I picked up the phone and didn’t hang up.  The person was offering me to be a beta test site for @home.  They said I would have 3 months of free internet service.  Like I said, it’s been over 3 years now, and I have never paid a cent to @home.  Even when AT&T bought them, I am still considered a vender, and don’t pay.   I love it….||||reg||10
Z||000022||kendall||05-25-2001||09:05 AM|||| When a carpet cleaning service calls act frantic and ask if they are able to get human blood out of the carpet, when they go into their spill about all the stains they can remove, get even more frantic and tell them that human blood coagulates in 12 minutes and they are wasting time they should get there right away. The tm will say that if you give add and info he can put you on the list for the following day, get extremely frantic and say "I will just do the best i can tonight because tomorrow I  will be a fugitive on the run and hang up. more than likely his/her supervisor will call back, have your wife/husband,girl/boy friend answer the phone and act if they are the only one at home and that the tm is crazy because the phone hasnt rang all evening||||reg||1
Z||000023||Formula||05-25-2001||09:27 AM||||hahaha<P>I'm a market researcher!  I've conducted the Soda survey before and honestly I prefer it when people say the same thing over and over, it makes it go quicker.  Also, if the researcher threw in his own question then that would be leading and he would get fired.  I usually only call the CEOs of dot com companies for business to business relations with microsoft.  But I do have to call residences if I work afternoon shift.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigformulagt.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000024||JSocha||05-25-2001||10:23 AM||||OMG!  Telemarketers <B>are</B> everywhere, even here!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000025||Will||05-25-2001||07:27 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fiero5:<BR><B>50 Fun Things To Do To Telemarketers<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>If the telemarketer is of the oposite sex, you could get some "pickup" practice.<P>A girl called me one time trying to sell me I-don't-remember-what. I flirted with her, struck up a conversation and invited her down to my apartment for the weekend.<P>Out of the blue she called back after she got off work that evening. She never came to my apartment, though...||||reg||1
Z||000026||Taijiguy||05-25-2001||08:31 PM||||The cemetary plot bit, and the carpet cleaning bit were donr by a guy named Tom Mabe. He's done a couple of CD's called "Revenge on the Telemarketers". The funniest bit he's done that I've heard was where he convinced the telemarketer calling him, that he was a standup comdian, and would the guy be willing to listen to his act. The guy agreed. So he proceded to tell a bunch of "stupid telemarketer" jokes. "Hey, why did the telemarketer cross the road?" "Why?" "To sell the chicken a bunch of crap he didn't need!" on and on he went....pretty soon the telemarketer was practically threatening to come over and kick his ass....too funny. The CD's are on sale all over the place, and MP3's are on napster I believe.||||reg||1
Z||000027||JSocha||05-25-2001||08:39 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Will:<BR><B>...Out of the blue she called back after she got off work that evening. She never came to my apartment, though...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><BR>Folks, I don't know about you...but that is a scary thought.<P>500 pounds of pure potential ugliness suddenly come to mind right off the bat if she had actually called back!<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||11
Z||000028||KissMySSFiero||05-26-2001||06:03 PM||||Anytime i get an "Unknow name" or someone i dont like or feel like messin with, i answer<BR>"Homosexuals Anonymous"   usually you get a short pause then hang up.   if i have the  number i like to call back.  hehe   "umm you just called us here.  I think its time you come out."||||reg||1
Z||000029||flipperwasaporpoise||05-28-2001||09:38 PM||||When GT Bastard and I still lived together, he did some really funny stuff.  Sometimes he would say he's deceased or ran away from home.  Other times he would meow (like a big, fat tom cat) or yell and hang up.  He really does sound like a cat.  I don't have the heart to do anything to telemarketers, so I just sit there and pretend to listen.  One time I was trying to listen, Jeff decides to turn up the TV as loud as it can go.  Then he started meowing REALLY loudly.  I couldn't hold it in the laughter.  Even the poor guy on the other end thought it was funny.||||reg||1
Z||000030||Taijiguy||05-29-2001||10:51 AM||||Here's one of Tom Mabe's bits. (only 650K MP3) <A HREF="http://members.core.com/~taijiguy/Files/Bob%20&%20Tom%20-%20Revenge%20On%20The%20Telemarketers%20-%20I%20Stabbed%20A%20Telemarketer.mp3" TARGET=_blank><B>I Stabbed a Telemarketer</B></A> <P><B>Try this one at home kids!</B><BR><p>[This message has been edited by Taijiguy (edited 05-29-2001).]||||reg||10
Z||000031||Fiero5||05-29-2001||10:59 AM||||"Homosexuals Anonymous" usually you get a short pause then hang up. if i have the number I like to call back. hehe "umm you just called us here. I think its time you come out."<P>ROTFL  I will have to try that one!<P>Steve<P>------------------<BR>                        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero9supersig_1.jpg">                      <BR>http://www.kelleyfamilyfieros.homestead.com/index.html||||reg||10
Z||000032||Tigger||05-29-2001||11:25 AM||||Where I use to work, some insurance company called one day.  Picked up the phone, "Hi, This is so and so from, yada, yada...."<P>All I said was "Sorry, we're not interested" and hung up the phone.<P>Few seconds later the phone rings again, pick it up, it's the so called supervisor of the telemarket place on the other end telling me he had monitored the call and was asking me why, what was said, or what caused me to not be interested.  What the????<P>Do You Understand?  I'm NOT interested!<P>A coworker and I joked about that one all that afternoon!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>If I have nothing much going on I'll just listen to their entire speal (may take 2-6 minutes or whatever), then just say "No, not interested."  Hehe, doesn't take long to hear the *click* on the other end.<P>Oh, a week or two ago I got one on a Sunday afternoon!  Talk about desperate!||||reg||1
